---
args: { prior: ObservatoryCheckpoint | null, request: CustomerObservatoryRequest, dossier: CustomerSignalDossier, episodes: EpisodeRegister, identities: IdentityVersionLedger, incidents: IncidentDedupLedger, concepts: StableProblemMap, trends: ComparableTrendSet | null, investigations: InvestigationQueue, consent: ConsentDerivativePlan, invalidations: ObservatoryInvalidation }
returns: ObservatoryCheckpoint
---
1. Bind consentEffects = reconcileConsentEffects(prior, request, dossier, consent, invalidations). Separate attributable quote removal from recomputation of restricted derivatives; retain non-attributable incidents and carry each absent external receipt as pending.
2. Bind trendLineage = reconcileTrendLineage(prior, request, incidents, concepts, trends, invalidations). Preserve exact windows whose cohort, channel, exposure, query and concept lineage still match; mark only dependent windows stale and keep their prior receipt editions.
3. For a null prior, create revision 1 for this case and store the supplied snapshot version, exact source versions and current episode, identity, incident, concept and investigation editions. Otherwise require the same case ID and preserve all earlier editions. If the snapshot and every consumed source version are already recorded, return the checkpoint unchanged. For a changed snapshot, append only editions whose evidence identity or interpretation changed; preserve prior source versions, incident groups, concept definitions and completed investigation evidence. Use consentEffects.pendingRemovalRefs and consentEffects.pendingRecomputeRefs for pending action history; never mark a proposed action complete. Use trendLineage.editionsToRetain as prior trend lineage. Retain unresolved identity effects. Advance revision once when any current edition, invalidation or pending effect changes; otherwise keep the revision.
